{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "guardians-follow-teleport-to-another-map",
  "contract": ["Summoned guardians come along on a teleport to another map, as a hearthstone or a portal makes: Player::TeleportTo to another map removes every guardian the player owns (Unit::RemoveFromWorld -> RemoveAllControlled -> UnSummon), and nothing makes them again. A real pet is carried by the core and is not part of this scenario.", "Players: An Undead Necromancer (class 23) with a Lesser Skeletal Warrior (500970, creature 50065) and a Ghoul (500971, creature 50073), 1 Life Force each, and an Orc Shaman with Feral Spirit (51533, two Spirit Wolves 29264, stock guardians that last 45 s and are summoned just before each travel). Counts are owned creatures within 100 yards (owned_creature_count); Life Force pool = stacks of 805011, free Life Force = stacks of 525004. Each check compares the value after a travel with a snapshot taken just before it, so the result does not depend on the pool size at level 20: the reported actual value is after minus before (for example -2 = two guardians lost).", "Each leg also asserts the absolute counts (one skeleton, one ghoul, two wolves) after the return, because the relative checks alone pass on a build that lost the guardians on the first leg: the second leg then starts with none. The teleport action calls the same Player::TeleportTo as the hearthstone and portal spell effects. Needs CoA.Guardians.FollowTravel = 1 (the default in coa.conf.dist). Expected: before the fix every check fails (-1 for each Necromancer kind, -2 for the wolves, +2 free Life Force); after it every check passes."],
  "timeout_ms": 240000,
  "location": {"map": 0, "x": 1676, "y": 1678, "z": 121, "o": 1.25},
  "players": [{"id": "necro", "race": 5, "class": 23, "level": 20, "security": 0}, {"id": "shaman", "race": 2, "class": 7, "level": 20, "security": 0}],
